            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le cauchemar comes from Old French cauquemare (EtymDB), built from caucher \"to press\", from Latin calcāre \"to tread\", and Middle Dutch mare \"a night ghost\", a Germanic word for a spirit that sits on the sleeper."
            }
          ]
